# Valgrind suppressions for Some Assembly Required
#
# ncurses allocates global state inside initscr() and keeps it for the
# life of the process. endwin() does not release all of it, by design.
# Valgrind reports those blocks as "possibly lost" or "still reachable".
#
# They are not our bugs and we cannot fix them -- but leaving them in the
# output trains you to skim past a report you should be reading closely.
# Suppress precisely these, and nothing else.
#
# Usage:  valgrind --suppressions=valgrind.supp ./game

{
   ncurses-initscr-tparm-setup
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible,reachable
   ...
   fun:initscr
   ...
}

{
   ncurses-newterm
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible,reachable
   ...
   fun:newterm
   ...
}

{
   ncurses-setupterm
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible,reachable
   ...
   fun:setupterm
   ...
}
